<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2023/9/eng@/~cl_6__para_a> <https://schema.org/text> "by substituting for subsection (2) the following subsection: “(2) The Director shall not issue a vocational licence unless he is satisfied that— (a) in the case of a licence to drive, the applicant is over the age of twenty-one; (b) in the case of a licence to act as a conductor, the applicant is over the age of eighteen; (c) the applicant is not a person holding a learner’s driving licence or a probationary driving licence; (d) in the case of an applicant who is a self-employed person, the applicant is registered and has paid the contribution under the Self-Employment Social Security Act 2017 [Act 789]; and (e) the applicant fulfils such other conditions as may be prescribed.”;"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2023/9/eng@> .
